#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:135
msgid "Local mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:137
msgid "**Local mode is available for self-hosted deployments only.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:139
msgid ""
"Local mode allows platform administrators with access to the Mattermost "
"server to run mmctl commands against the API without needing to have a "
"user registered. To ensure secure usage of this API, the server exposes a"
" local socket that only a user with access to the server's file system "
"can access. The requests coming from the socket are treated as "
"authorized, so they can reach the handlers without requiring a user "
"session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:141
msgid ""
"The API that the socket exposes follows the same specification that can "
"be found `in the API documentation <https://api.mattermost.com>`_, so "
"mmctl is able to interact with it without needing any modifications. When"
" a request comes in through the socket, it is flagged as local by the "
"server, and this flag is taken into account when checking for session "
"permissions to correctly authorize the sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:144
msgid "Activating local mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:146
msgid ""
"To use local mode, the Mattermost server first needs to :ref:`have local "
"mode enabled <administration-guide/configure/experimental-configuration-"
"settings:enable local mode for mmctl>`. When local mode is enabled, a "
"socket is created at ``/var/tmp/mattermost_local.socket`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:150
msgid ""
"When trying to use local mode with mmctl, ensure you're using the same "
"user when running the server and mmctl, or clean up the socket file "
"before switching to a new user. If you encounter an error like ``socket "
"file \"/var/tmp/mattermost_local.socket\" doesn't exists, please check "
"the server configuration for local mode``, this can be resolved by "
"setting this configuration setting to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:153
msgid "Using local mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:155
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.8, when no authentication credentials are found in "
"the authentication configuration, mmctl automatically assumes local mode,"
" eliminating the need to manually append the ``--local`` flag to the "
"command you want to use. When valid credentials exist, Mattermost will "
"continue to validate them as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:157
msgid ""
"Prior to Mattermost v10.8, you must append ``--local`` to the command you"
" want to use, or set the environment variable as ``MMCTL_LOCAL=true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool.rst:159
msgid ""
"To use a socket file other than the default, you need to set the "
"environment variable to ``MMCTL_LOCAL_SOCKET_PATH``. This file must match"
" the :ref:`server configuration setting <administration-guide/configure"
"/experimental-configuration-settings:enable local mode socket location>`."
msgstr ""

